Z||000010||fldevel||03-07-2001||03:05 PM||||well that lil tube that goes from the intake to the valve thingy on the top of my Y pipe has a leak in it .. never did this untill i replaced the watter pump .. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||87GT||03-07-2001||08:22 PM||||I had the exact same problem so I took it to my cousins to have checked out and it showed up on his scanner that it was the 02 Sensor, and EGR Diagnostics, which when one has a prob, the other usually shows as a prob as well.  Turns out to be a part of the EGR that he has to order from Georgia.  I think it may have been the selonoid but Im not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Bob Englert||03-07-2001||10:44 PM||||On my blue 87 GT I had the same problem it turned out to be the EGR Solenoid.  <P>On my maroon GT I didn't have any high idle but the EGR didn't appear to be functioning.  When I lifted the EGR diaphram the engine didn't react at all.  When I went to check the tube I found the tube broken in 2 near the valve but the tube was completely plugged up at the plenum.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
